  "transcript": "Amazon's growth engine is one of the most famous flywheels in business. Let's break it down. It starts with the customer base — Prime members. As customers grow, they generate more traffic. More traffic attracts third-party sellers onto the marketplace. Those sellers expand the product selection. A wider selection improves the customer experience. And better experience drives new member signups, feeding the customer base again. But there's another force: scale enables lower prices, which also drives signups. This is the virtuous cycle that turned an online bookstore into the everything store.",
